From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: Import into the KMS device only when a KMS handle
 is asked for

With a renderonly display, panfrost_resource_from_handle() imports every
dma-buf it is given into the KMS device, in case a KMS handle is asked
for later. A compositor imports each client buffer to sample from it and
never asks, so every import also attaches the buffer to the display.

On a display without an IOMMU that has a 32-bit DMA mask, as mediatek-drm
on the MT6789 with 12 GiB of RAM, most client buffers lie above 4 GiB.
Mapping them for the display bounces them through swiotlb: a buffer with
a segment larger than swiotlb's 256 KiB limit fails with "swiotlb buffer
is full", one with smaller segments is copied, and when the copy happens
to be contiguous the import succeeds and keeps the bounce buffer for the
life of the texture. None of these is a buffer the display could scan
out.

Make the import on the first KMS handle request instead, as
renderonly_get_handle() is the only user of the scanout for an imported
resource. gbm_bo_import() followed by gbm_bo_get_handle() still gets a
KMS handle; sampling an imported buffer no longer touches the display.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
index 30b59e2..afe7b39 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -437,12 +437,6 @@ panfrost_resource_from_handle(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
    BITSET_SET(rsc->valid.data, 0);
    panfrost_resource_set_damage_region(pscreen, &rsc->base, 0, NULL);
 
-   if (dev->ro) {
-      rsc->scanout =
-         renderonly_create_gpu_import_for_resource(prsc, dev->ro, NULL);
-      /* failure is expected in some cases.. */
-   }
-
    return prsc;
 }
 
@@ -488,6 +482,10 @@ panfrost_resource_get_handle(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
    rsrc->modifier_constant = true;
 
    if (handle->type == WINSYS_HANDLE_TYPE_KMS && dev->ro) {
+      /* Import into the KMS device only once a KMS handle is asked for. */
+      if (!scanout)
+         scanout = rsrc->scanout =
+            renderonly_create_gpu_import_for_resource(pt, dev->ro, NULL);
       return renderonly_get_handle(scanout, handle);
    } else if (handle->type == WINSYS_HANDLE_TYPE_KMS) {
       handle->handle = panfrost_bo_handle(rsrc->bo);
-- 
